    Layout = null;
}
    <link href="~/css/advocateempanelment/letter.css" rel="stylesheet" />

    <div class="container">
        <div class="button-container">
            <button class="print-button" id="print1">
                <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                    <polyline points="6 9 6 2 18 2 18 9"></polyline>
                    <path d="M6 18H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h16a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v5a2 2 0 0 1-2 2h-2"></path>
                    <rect x="6" y="14" width="12" height="8"></rect>
                </svg>
                Print Letter
            </button>
            <button class="exit-button" id="exitBtn">
                <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                    <line x1="18" y1="6" x2="6" y2="18"></line>
                    <line x1="6" y1="6" x2="18" y2="18"></line>
                </svg>
                Exit
            </button>
        </div>

        <div class="letter-content" id="printArea">
            <p class="text-right"><strong>Empanelment Letter</strong></p>
            <p class="text-right">26-May-2025</p>

            <p style="margin-top: 20px;"><strong>Nyaydristi Advocates and Solicitors</strong></p>
        <p id="name"> </p>
        <p id="address"> </p><br /><br />

            <p>Dear Sir/Madam,</p>

            <p><strong><span class="underline">Subject: Engagement as Panel Advocate</span></strong></p>

            <p>
                This has reference to the discussions we had and your proposal for rendering services as a Panel Advocate for our Company.
                In this regard, we are glad to engage you in our panel on the following terms and conditions.
            </p>

            <div class="section-title">Appointment and Scope of Work:</div>
            <p>
                You shall provide the Services as set out in Annexure-I here to, together with such other works/assignments
                the Company may from time to time inform you.
            </p>

            <div class="section-title">Non-exclusive and Principal to Principal:</div>
            <p>
                The appointment is on a non-exclusive basis and is on a principal-to-principal basis. Further, you shall only
                perform all the services as detailed in the appointment letter and shall not assign, transfer, or sub-contract
                any of its rights and obligations under this appointment letter except with the prior written permission of the Company.
            </p>

            <div class="section-title">Advocate's Covenants:</div>
            <p>
                The said Services rendered, and obligations performed by you pursuant to this appointment letter would be with
                utmost care and diligence and shall be of the highest quality and standards. If at any time, the Company is
                dissatisfied with the service rendered by you, the Company may, without notice, terminate this contract with
                immediate effect. The Company's decision in this regard shall be final, absolute, and binding on you.
            </p>
            <p>
                All documents and other informatory papers including negotiable instruments and any other documents relating to
                all company's products, schemes, accounts, etc., ("hereinafter referred to as "the Documents") handed over to
                you or your staff by the company shall remain the sole and absolute property of the company, and you shall not
                have any charge claim, lien, right of retention, sale or set-off or other right, title or interest therein or
                thereon for any reason whatsoever. You shall, at all times, maintain and respect the confidentiality of all/any
                matters relating to the Service under this Agreement. This Agreement does not create any employer-employee
                relationship between yourself and the company, and no such claim shall be made by you to the company during the
                tenure of the relationship. Further, you will not appear in any court of law, tribunal, forum etc. against the company.
            </p>

            <div class="section-title">Mode of Communication:</div>
            <p>
                Prescribed mode of communication of all necessary information, documents, next posting date, current proceedings,
                etc. shall be only done preferably through e-mails and no other modes of communication. It is also mandatory that
                all the details of the respective court proceedings be sent to the Branch Head by end of that particular day itself
                through email. An exclusive email ID solely for the communication with respect to the matter of the company also
                need to be created.
            </p>

            <div class="section-title">Attendance of Court Proceedings:</div>
            <p>
                For each and every court proceeding of the cases that involves our company, it is mandatory that you, personally
                or any competent advocate from your office, would attend the proceedings and it is solely your responsibility.
                In a situation where the proceedings go unattended, any cost that incurs due to such delay in the court proceedings
                shall be borne by you.
            </p>

            <div class="section-title">Termination:</div>
            <p>
                Asirvad Micro Finance Ltd and You, as a company advocate, shall have the right to terminate this appointment by
                giving 15 days' notice in writing without assigning reason thereof. Upon the receipt of termination letter, you
                shall cease to appear as Advocate for and behalf of the company in all matters and also refrain yourself from any
                action that would or may impair the relationship between you and company.
            </p>
            <p>
                On termination of your services, without any demur, you shall forthwith handed over all brief, documents, statements
                and all other material held by you in the capacity of Lawyer of the company and obtain receipts for the same. You
                shall provide a "No Objection" on your letter head and to engage the services of any other or more lawyers and also
                perform all such activities for smooth transfer of matters from you to others.
            </p>

            <div class="section-title">Fee Structure:</div>
            <p>
                In consideration of the services to be provided by you, the Company shall pay an all-inclusive charge as mentioned
                in ANNEXURE-II to this letter. Any legal options sought would not be charged separately, this will include oral
                options and written options. Your professional services shall be availed on purely a 'need basis' and no fixed
                periodical payment shall be made by the company to you for the professional services rendered.
            </p>

            <p>
                We are sending this letter in duplicate, kindly sign the duplicate letter and forward to us as a token of acceptance
                of all the terms and conditions.
            </p>

            <p>Looking forward to a long and fruitful relationship.</p>

            <div class="signature-section">
                <div class="signature-block">
                    <p><strong>Regards,</strong></p>
                    <p><strong>Asirvad Micro Finance Ltd</strong></p>
                    <div class="signature-space"></div>
                    <p>_____________________</p>
                    <p>Head Legal</p>
                    <p>Date: ______________</p>
                </div>
                <div class="signature-block">
                    <p><strong>Accepted By</strong></p>
                    <div class="signature-space"></div>
                    <p>_____________________</p>
                    <p>Name: ______________</p>
                    <p>Place: ______________</p>
                    <p>Date: ______________</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
<script nonce="5d67de6751aa4e158c33dfd828fc144b">
    document.getElementById('address').textContent ='addd';
              document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function() {
                      function getQueryParam(param) {
       var urlParams = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search);
       return urlParams.get(param);
    }
               // document.getElementById('address').textContent=window.adv;

               document.getElementById('address').textContent=getQueryParam('address')+ ",";
                document.getElementById('name').textContent=getQueryParam('fullname')+ ",";
              // const advocateId = urlParams.get('id');
                  // let address=documnet
            const printButton = document.getElementById('print1');
            const exitButton = document.getElementById('exitBtn');

            if (printButton) {
                printButton.addEventListener('click', function() {
                    try {
                        window.print();
                    } catch (error) {
                        console.error('Print error:', error);
                        alert('Unable to print. Please use your browser\'s print function (Ctrl+P).');
                    }
                });
            }

            if (exitButton) {
                exitButton.addEventListener('click', function() {
                    window.close();
                    setTimeout(function() {
                        if (typeof redirectToDashboard === 'function') {
                            redirectToDashboard();
                        } else {
                            window.history.back();
                        }
                    }, 100);
                });
            }
        });
</script>

